<Doc lang={lang} page="blocks" current="Gradient" title="Gradient"
  description="The Gradient block of FLOAT: three models of the sky gradient (polynomial, RBF, automatic), the samples of sky, the H-alpha survey that keeps samples off the nebulosity, and the settings.">

  <p class="kicker">Block</p>
  <h1>Gradient</h1>
  <p class="meta">FLOAT 0.2.0 · beta of {release.date.en}</p>

  <dl class="inshort"><div><dt>What it does</dt><dd>It takes off the uneven glow that light pollution and the Moon spread over the image, so that the sky background is even from one edge to the other.</dd></div><div><dt>What it shows</dt><dd>In Inspect, the stack with the gradient removed, with the size of the gradient (in % of the sky level) and the number of sky samples used; the same figure in the Report.</dd></div><div><dt>What can be set</dt><dd>The Method: Polynomial (the default) suits most fields, Automatic follows more complex gradients; and the Surface degree (2), raised to 3 or 4 for wide fields.</dd></div></dl>

  <aside class="note toc">
